// Title: Amsi.DLL Loaded Via LOLBIN Process
// Sigma ID: 6ec86d9e-912e-4726-91a2-209359b999b9
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-01 | Modified: 2025-10-07
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment
// Description: Detects loading of "Amsi.dll" by a living of the land process. This could be an indication of a
//   "PowerShell without PowerShell" attack
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - Internal Research
//   - https://www.paloaltonetworks.com/blog/security-operations/stopping-powershell-without-powershell/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_dll_amsi_suspicious_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\amsi.dll" and (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ExtExport.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\odbcconf.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe")
